# Documentation

Follow grokbotsrules `docs-rules.md`.

## This repo

Short file map (PED Toolbox, branch `v3`):

- `README.md` — what it is, how to run it
- `docs/CHANGELOG.md` — dated product notes, newest first; will align with fleet release evidence (P0 risk effect, artifact SHA256/size when built)
- `docs/HISTORY.md` — per-version finished work; together with `CHANGELOG.md` this repo’s CHANGELOG/HISTORY pair until folded into one file later
- `docs/TASKS.md` — **task index today** (links to detail files); keeps current status keys (`todo` / `waiting` / `later` / `done`) until the BACKLOG migration PR, then switches to fleet keys; will be folded into `docs/BACKLOG.md` in a later PR
- `docs/ROADMAP.md` — milestones, done vs later
- `docs/RISKS.md` — `R-n` risks; status open/accepted/mitigated/closed; Impact; Likelihood; Decision
- `docs/RELEASING.md` — release runbook, no secrets
- `docs/TEAM.md` — people and bots, merge flow
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` — folders, how actions run
- `docs/FEATURES.md` — page-by-page behavior
- `docs/PACKAGING.md` — winget and Microsoft Store packaging
- `docs/DOWNLOAD.md` — program zip vs source
- `docs/RUN.md` — build and run locally
- `docs/ANALYSIS.md` — v1/v2/v3 rationale
- `docs/tasks/<ID>.md` — task detail (this project uses **`docs/tasks/`**, not `docs/specs/`); Goal / Done / Still waiting / **Do not**
- `docs/PROJECT.md` — **planned** (product, audience, locked decisions)
- `docs/BACKLOG.md` — **planned** (single task index with Who acts)
- `docs/archive/` — **planned** (legacy files + `README.md`; archive, don’t delete)

Task ids use the `T-n` scheme (e.g. `T032-2`).

1. Product owns the docs. Every change: PR → Review → Product go → merge. Never push to `v3` directly.
2. One id scheme per project (`T-n`). Two-layer ids allowed if declared at the top of `BACKLOG.md` when it exists. Never reuse or renumber ids, and never delete rows.
3. Same status keys in every file: proposed, next, doing, merged (unreleased), shipped in X, deferred, superseded -> ID, done, waiting (external: X). RISKS: open, accepted, mitigated, closed.
4. Shipped: app projects need the GitHub release (version/code, date, release URL, build SHA). Built artifacts: SHA256 and size next to the build SHA.
5. Update docs in the same PR as the change, plus a docs PR after every release. Each file keeps a dated Status as of line.
6. CHANGELOG/HISTORY is newest-first, dated and append-only. Each entry includes what was intentionally not done and the effect on open P0 risks (e.g. R-1 unchanged). Bilingual CHANGELOG allowed.
7. Record Pier's decisions with a date in PROJECT or RISKS. Never change them without him.
8. No new loose PLAN-*, STATUS-* or dated CHANGELOG-* files; detail goes in `docs/tasks/<ID>.md`. Move legacy files to `docs/archive/` when that folder exists. No secrets or binaries in docs.
9. Task detail files: Goal / Done / Still waiting / **Do not** (Do not = scope limits for bots; required).
10. Plain language: explain each term on first use, in the project's working language (English here).
11. ROADMAP: success criteria + owner gate. Next phase starts only after Product (and Pier when needed) reviews.
12. BACKLOG: Who acts column, or Pier vs bot queues (when `BACKLOG.md` exists).
